<title>USA: Ryan, Beck CEO resigns, Q4 charge seen.</title>
<headline>Ryan, Beck CEO resigns, Q4 charge seen.</headline>
<dateline>WEST ORANGE, N.J. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ryan, Beck &amp; Co Inc said Allen Greene resigned as president and chief executive, which will cause the company to take an after-tax charge of $420,000, or $0.13 per share, in the fourth quarter to cover the cost of severance and employment costs.</p>
<p>The company said Greene resigned to pursue personal interests.  </p>
<p>The company said it has created a senior management committee to execute oversight duties.</p>
<p>Ben Plotkin, formerly senior executive vice president, was named president of the company and chairman of the management committee.</p>
